So v4/v5 still misclassify f=890-1050 as FOUNTAIN (62 frames) when it should be CASCADE. The detector signal alone isn't enough — the late phase has balls moving in the same horizontal direction, which is actually consistent with a juggler mid-cascade (during the throw-and-catch transition, multiple balls can move same direction).

This is an important finding: the detector-level vx-direction signal is also limited, just for a different reason. The juggler can be in a CASCADE pattern and still have many frames where balls move in the same horizontal direction (mid-arc). This is a known limitation of the vx-IQR approach for pattern recognition.

