+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""H13 - Low-confidence detector corroboration of hand events (master §14, v2).
+
+Hypothesis: for each v4d hand-link AND each H7v2-reclassified edge,
+scan a wider temporal window for low-conf sports-ball detections
+WITHIN REACH of the relevant hand. If they exist, the hand-link is
+"corroborated" by detector evidence (even if the gap spans detector
+dropouts).
+
+This extends H3 (which only considered v4d hand-links) to H7v2
+reclassified edges too. H13 is the *full* test of master §14.
+
+Thresholds (declared before reading outcomes):
+- HAND_REACH_PX = 108 (same as v2/v4/H7v2)
+- LOW_CONF_THRESHOLD = 0.5
+- GAP_PAD_FRAMES = 5  (extend window beyond the gap by 5 frames each side)
+- MIN_LOW_CONF_NEEDED = 1  (single detection is enough signal)
+- MAX_GAP_FRAMES = 60  (don't bother with gaps > 60 frames; detector
+  dropout is more likely than missed catch-throw)
+
+Output: per-edge corroboration summary + CSV.
+
+Three classes per edge:
+- CORROBORATED: ≥1 low-conf sports ball detection within reach
+  of the hand during the gap + 2*pad frames
+- NO_EVIDENCE: no low-conf detections in the search window
+- REFUTED: ≥3 low-conf sports ball detections far from hand
+  (suggesting the edge is in a wrong region)
