Interesting findings! The v3 concentration test (n_in >= 3 AND n_in >= n_out) never fires — there are always more low-conf dets OUT of reach than in reach. The detector sees the whole frame; the hand is just one small area. This is a real negative result.

But the AVG concentration tells an interesting story:
- v4d avg concentration: 0.150 (15% of low-conf dets are near the hand)
- h7v2_reclassified avg concentration: 0.268 (27%)

So h7v2-reclassified edges have a higher concentration of low-conf detections at the hand than v4d links! This is a real signal that supports the H7v2 reclassification interpretation (more held-ball evidence at these locations).

Let me think about this more carefully. The n_in >= n_out criterion is too strict because the hand region is small (108px radius circle) compared to the full frame. The right comparison is: do hand-link windows have HIGHER concentration than random hand-region windows?

