╭─ ⚕ Hermes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
This is the key finding! The h7v2-reclassified edges have a higher median concentration than v4d links (identical: 0.17 vs 0.14, youtube: 0.29 vs 0.23). This suggests the detector DOES preferentially fire at h7v2-reclassified edges more than at v4d hand-links — even though neither is "concentrated" in the absolute sense.

This makes physical sense: h7v2 reclassified edges are BALLISTIC edges that pass through a hand region, and the ball really is at the hand, so the detector has more low-conf evidence there. v4d links are hand-only events (catch+throw pairs) where the ball is often fully in the hand and occluded.

