The vision tool's analysis is very interesting but it's also a bit over-interpretive. The 46 in-reach detections are NOT 46 in 6 frames — they're spread over the full 11-frame window. Looking at the panel annotations, I can see the conf labels 0.74, 0.37, 0.32 in the hand region. The tool is suggesting the hand-region confs aren't dramatically higher than background.

This is actually a useful scientific finding: H7v2's reclassification rule is more permissive than the detector evidence alone supports. H7v2 uses geometric rules (distance + slope + gap ≤ 20) to reclassify, but the detector signal is essentially the same for reclassified and kept-ballistic edges. The geometric rules are doing the work, not the detector.

This is consistent with the finding: h7v2_reclassified and h7v2_kept_ballistic have similar concentration (0.201 vs 0.206) on identical. The detector doesn't strongly distinguish them.

