The chain 20 decrease is interesting. Let me check what happened there. Chain 20 is [30, 33] with 1 V_RECLASSIFIED edge. In v8, it had n_hand=0, n_air=1, h8=1.00 (no violation). In v9, it has n_hand=1, n_air=0, h8=1.00, v_reclass=1.

The h3 weight is 0.30 for identical. v8 had h3=None (no hand edges) so the weights were re-balanced. v9 has h3=0 (1 hand edge but no h3 confirmation) which is worse than None.

This is a design choice in h10. When h3=None (no hand edges), the algorithm redistributes the h3 weight to other dimensions. But when h3=0 (hand edges but no confirmation), the algorithm uses h3=0 which is a real signal.

