The cleanest discriminator: does the tgt's first detection have a distance > some_threshold from the V-apex hand? Because a real throw has the ball receding from the hand at the moment of the first detection (so d > reach), while a tracklet break or hand-borne has the tgt's first detection either very close to the hand (held/oscillating) or not at the hand at all (mid-air start).

