Let me design H17: parabolic-physics consistency on the gap trajectory. The hypothesis: a real catch+throw's gap trajectory follows TWO parabolic arcs (catch parabola ending at the hand, throw parabola starting at the hand). The HAND position should be at the apex of both arcs. A tracklet break or mid-air continuation has the gap trajectory as a SINGLE parabola, with no apex at the hand.

The check: fit parabolas to src-tail (catch parabola) and tgt-head (throw parabola); check that both predict an apex at the V-apex hand position. If yes → catch+throw. If only one (or neither) → not a clean catch+throw.

Actually, even simpler: the H14 V-shape check already finds the V-apex. The new H17 check is: does the velocity direction at the V-apex change sign? A real catch+throw has the ball moving toward the hand before the apex, then away after. A hand-borne has the ball staying near the hand (low |velocity|). A tracklet break has the ball suddenly jumping in some direction.

Let me formalize this as the velocity-direction-change check at the V-apex:
- Compute vrad (radial velocity toward V-apex hand) for src tail and tgt head
- A real catch+throw: src_vrad < 0 (approaching), tgt_vrad > 0 (receding) — the velocity DIRECTION CHANGED at the V-apex
- A hand-borne: src_vrad < 0 (approaching), tgt_vrad < 0 (still approaching) — NO direction change, ball continues toward hand
- A tracklet break: src_vrad ≈ 0 (stationary at hand), tgt_vrad > 0 (receding) — src is stationary, tgt jumps away

