- 39→47: HAND-BORNE (ball carried from face to chest)
- 51→52: REAL CATCH+THROW (left→right handoff)
- 27→28: FALSE POSITIVE (tracklet break)

What if I look at it from yet another angle: does the ball change direction in the trajectory? A real catch+throw has the ball moving TOWARD the hand (src tail), then at the V-apex (the catch point), the ball STOPS or moves slightly differently, then it moves AWAY (tgt head). A tracklet break has the ball moving smoothly in one direction (no direction change at the apex).

