- 35,37,RECLASSIFIED_HAND_TRANSITION and 37,40,RECLASSIFIED_HAND_TRANSITION (chain 23)

So the h7v2 reclassification rule (which checks endpoint distance AND slope) is more permissive than v4d's hand-pool rule. The 15→25 case has src_catch_dist=6.6 (well within 108) and slope=-2.08 (catches with |slope| >= 1.0 but v4d's threshold is 2.5). v4d requires the catch slope to be steep; h7v2 only requires >= 1.0. So the h7v2 rule already recovered both v4d-rejected cases.

This is an important insight for H17: The 2 v4d-rejected links that the V-shape strict check recovers are ALREADY in the h7v2 chain as RECLASSIFIED edges. H17's V-shape + strict check is just an alternative path to the same conclusion.

