So H17 finds genuine new candidates in e6c_not_in_h7v2, but the precision is ~30-50% — much lower than h7v2's ~80% precision on the reclassified edges.

The takeaway: H17's strict V-shape is a useful research tool for finding candidates that h7v2 missed, but applying it as a chain reclassifier would introduce many false positives. The current h7v2 endpoint check (dist + slope) is a more conservative and precise filter.

