The remaining 3 FPs (35→38, 10→11, 1→10) are characterized by:
- Source IS in the hand (src_inhand=True) 
- Target is NOT in the hand (tgt_inhand=False)
- The V-shape apex is just the source position in the hand, not a real catch+throw

A natural extension: reject if the source is in the hand AND the V-apex is also at the source hand (no catch+throw occurred; the apex is just the source position). Let me also check the V-apex vs source-end relationship:

Actually, looking at the data: for these 3 FPs, src_inhand=True but tgt_inhand=False. The ball is sitting in the hand (source) and then appears elsewhere (target). The V-apex lands at the source hand because the source endpoint is right there.

A cleaner check: REJECT if the source's last frame and the V-apex are at the SAME hand (i.e., the V-apex is just the source's last position, not a real catch). This would catch 35→38, 1→10 where the source is in the hand and the V-apex is at the source hand.

