Wait, let me re-check. The "V-apex" in H17 logic is the trajectory point CLOSEST to the hand. For a real catch+throw, the apex should be in the gap (where the ball is at the hand), not necessarily in the source or target. But the H17 V-apex could be ANY point on the trajectory (source, gap interpolation, or target). If the target is high up (above the hand), then the target point is closer to the hand than the source which is even higher... no, that doesn't make sense.

Let me re-read the H17 V-apex logic carefully. The trajectory includes source tail, gap interpolation, and target head. The V-apex is the point closest to the hand. For 13→15 (REAL):
- Source (tracklet 13) goes from (526, 438) to (422, 446) — descending leftward at f=134-138
- Target (tracklet 15) goes from (526, 491) to (532, 572) at f=138-142 — moving down-right
