This is a powerful finding: the H32 per-chain CASCADE/FOUNTAIN classification based on hand-alternation is fundamentally confounded by multi-ball merges. A "CASCADE_LIKE" hand sequence (L→L→R→R→L) doesn't mean a single ball did a cascade — it could mean 3 different balls were juggled, each tracklet getting one hand.

This is actually consistent with what H11 (identity propagation) showed: the chain set is largely multi-ball. The h7v3plus2 chains are mostly fragmented detections of multiple balls, not single-ball juggling cycles.

