This is itself an important finding: the chain construction (H7v2 + H15v2 + H21 + H26) does not produce tracklet overlaps even when the chain represents multiple physical balls. This is because:
- Hand-edges (HAND_TRANSITION, RECLASSIFIED, etc.) require a catch-throw, which means source ends before target starts.
- BALLISTIC edges link two tracklets that are temporally adjacent (one ends, next starts).

So the chain is by construction temporally sequential. Multi-ball merges happen because the content of the tracklets (which physical ball) doesn't follow the chain's structure, not because the chain has overlapping tracklets.

