H40 (PASS): Continuous per-frame hand-occupancy signal from raw detector + pose. v2 (sustained 100 px, 3-frame run) detects 3-4x more hand-occupancy than H36 (72.3% vs 23.7% on identical, 98.1% vs 25.8% on YouTube). Useful diagnostic.

H41 (NEGATIVE): FOUNTAIN_3+ post-filter via H40 v2. Same precision as H39 v2 (50%) — no improvement.

H42 (MIXED): Hybrid H36 + H40 v2 (L, R, A) state. Fills 51-73% of HOLD frames with H40 occupancy, but doesn't improve CASCADE/FOUNTAIN discrimination.

H43 (PASS, narrow scope): H12 v8 confidence-based FOUNTAIN_3+ filter. Rejects 9.1% of identical FOUNTAIN_3+ (lowest confidence) with 100% precision. The most reliable FOUNTAIN_3+ post-filter tested. H43 + h7v3plus3 is the new recommended operating point.

H44 (literature search): Web search confirms no prior CV-based cascade/fountain classification work. Most related is 3D ball trajectory estimation (Ponglertnapakorn 2025, physics-based 2009/2012). Siteswap notation is well-defined (Büttiken et al. 2024 arXiv:2410.19591) but not a CV problem.

Key insight from this session: H12 v8's own confidence is the most reliable signal for FOUNTAIN_3+ misclassifications. External signals (H36 chain events, H40 sustained-occupancy) are too noisy to beat H12 v8's calibrated self-confidence.

All artifacts committed and pushed to origin/experiments/hand-occlusion-overnight. 5 new reports (h39_report.md, h40_h41_report.md, h42_report.md, h43_report.md) plus RESEARCH_NOTES cross-cutting insights 36-48.
