+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""H46: per-flight physics check via H8 v8.
+
+HYPOTHESIS:
+  H45 found that H12 v8 hand-event "flights" include both real
+  catch-throws (30-40 frame flight times on identical) and
+  tracker-fragmentation artifacts (1-5 frame "flights" on
+  identical, 58-134 frame "flights" on YouTube). The
+  distinguishing feature is physical consistency: a real
+  catch-throw has the source's last arc and target's first
+  arc on a continuous physical trajectory. A tracker
+  fragmentation has them physically disconnected (slope
+  jump, position jump, etc.).
+
+  H8 v8 already computes per-arc parabolic fits (gravity
+  estimate, v0, y0). For each H12 v8 flight:
+    1. Take the source tracklet's last arc
+    2. Take the target tracklet's first arc
+    3. Extrapolate source's last arc to target's first
+       observed frame, given the gap (no ball observed)
+    4. Compare predicted (x, y) to actual target's first
+       (x, y)
+    5. If position error > THRESHOLD, classify as
+       PHYSICS_VIOLATION (likely tracker fragmentation)
+
+  Real catch-throws should have small position errors
+  (the ball continues on the same parabola through the
+  unobserved hold phase). Tracker fragmentations should
+  have large position errors (the re-acquired ball is in
+  a different place than where the parabola predicted).
+
+ALGORITHM:
+  1. Load h45_siteswap_flights.csv (H12 v8 flights).
+  2. For each flight, load source and target tracklet
+     points from detections/<stem>_norfair_dt50_hc5.csv.
+  3. Detect extrema in source's last 1/3 of points
+     and target's first 1/3 of points; use the last
+     arc of source and first arc of target.
+  4. Fit parabola y = 0.5*g*t^2 + v0*t + y0 to each arc.
+  5. Predict y at target's first frame using source's
+     last-arc parabola extrapolated across the gap.
+  6. Compare predicted y to actual y at target's first frame.
+  7. Compare predicted x using source's last-arc vx (constant).
+  8. Score:
+       - position error dx, dy
+       - ratio of position error to source's last 5-frame
+         x/y velocity (a relative error measure)
+  9. Cross-validate against the 11 H45 visually-confirmed
+     flights: 7 REAL (3-ball identical), 4 IDENTITY SWITCH/
+     TRACKER FRAGMENTATION (1, 5, 58, 61, 62, 134 frames).
+
+  THRESHOLD: declared from physics, not labels.
+    - A real catch-throw's source-last-arc parabola can
+      extrapolate across a 30-40 frame gap and predict
+      target's first y within ~30 pixels (1-2 ball diameters).
+    - A tracker fragmentation has 100+ pixel error.
+    - Default POSITION_ERROR_THRESHOLD = 50 px.
+
+NOT parameter-tuned. Thresholds declared from physical
+geometry, not from manual labels.
+"""
