Interesting! The H50 timeline has 22 CATCH->THROW pairs and 10 of them have gap_frames < 10. But the CATCH->next CATCH pairs (which my H53b uses) don't have any short flights. The H50 report's "10 short flights" refers to gap_frames (CATCH->THROW), not flight_time (CATCH->next CATCH).

Wait, the H50 report says "10/1042 (1.0%) frames changed" on identical and dropped "6 events" but the timeline shows 10 short CATCH->THROW pairs. The H50 report's "10 frames" is the per-frame pattern label change, not the event count.

Looking at the h50_dropped_events file, it only has 3 dropped pairs (the 3 with flight_time<10). But there are 10 CATCH->THROW pairs with gap_frames<10. So "flight_time" in the H50 events file is gap_frames (which is CATCH->THROW same-chain), not the CATCH->next CATCH distance. The H50 filter is CATCH->THROW gap<10, not CATCH->next CATCH gap<10.

