Now I see the full picture. The H12 v8 event log has each (CATCH, THROW) pair with the same tid and prev_tid because it's tracking the ball's lifecycle WITHIN a single tracklet. The CATCH frame is when the tracklet first enters the hand region; the THROW frame is when the tracklet leaves the hand region. The "gap_frames" is the held-phase duration. The H12 v8 chain_events file shows frame as 0/1/2 (chain-internal event index, not actual frame number).

So the H53b comparison is using the wrong pairing. The H52 physics check on H12 v8 events should check the previous tracklet's tail + held-phase + current tracklet's head, NOT the same tracklet's CATCH-frame and THROW-frame. The from_tid and to_tid in the H12 v8 events ARE the same tracklet.

For a proper H52-vs-H50 comparison, I need to use the actual tracklet-level pairs: the CATCH is at the END of prev_tid tracklet, the THROW is at the START of the current tid tracklet. The H12 v8 prev_tid is what I should use as source, and the current tid as target.

