2. Multi-rater visual QA consensus: all 3 dropped pairs are TRACKER_FRAGMENTATION (3/3 or 2/3 + tie).
3. H52+MIN=2 is over-aggressive on the full event log (19/25 identical, 24/25 YouTube). The 10-frame filter is more conservative.
4. H50-only drops (6 identical, 1 YouTube) include both real catch-throws and the chain 23 ft=1 ambiguity case. H52 sees "OK" or "INSUFFICIENT_DATA" on these — the parabolic check doesn't catch them.

The H52+MIN=2 is not a viable standalone filter, but it's a useful corroborating signal: when an H50 drop also has H52 VIOLATING, that's high-confidence fragmentation. When an H50 drop has H52 OK or INSUFFICIENT_DATA, the case is ambiguous.

